quiet.md #22: read text and one image from the macOS pasteboard

Upstream returns the first kind it recognises (files, then a string, then an
image). Screenshot tools put both an image and a text fallback on the
pasteboard; return the string and one image (PNG before TIFF) so the document
can take the image while text fields still read the text. Empty image data is
skipped. Tested on private pasteboards (pasteboard::tests).

